NAME
       strace - graphical system call tracer

SYNOPSIS
       strace

DESCRIPTION
       Shows the system calls of a process tree live, using the kernel
       tracing facility. Start a command with the entry and Start button, or
       choose Attach to PID to pick a running process from a list. Kernel
       threads, PID 1 and the tracer itself cannot be traced, and a normal
       user can only trace their own processes. Forked children are followed
       and shown as nested nodes.

       The main area is a tree. Every process is a node with its PID, name,
       state and counters; click it, or press Left and Right, to collapse
       or expand it. Under a node are its system calls, with decoded
       arguments, the result (errors in red with the error name) and the
       duration (slow calls in yellow), and the nodes of its child processes.
       Autoscroll keeps the newest rows in view and switches off when you
       scroll up. At most 50000 rows are kept, the oldest are dropped.

       The Details tab shows all arguments of the selected call, raw and
       decoded, the string argument, result, duration and kernel timestamp.
       The Statistics tab draws a bar chart of the calls of the selected
       process; the red part of a bar is failed calls.

       Toolbar:
           Pause     freeze the display; events are still collected
           Detach    stop tracing, the processes keep running
           Clear     detach and remove all rows
           Filter    show only calls whose name or string contains the text
           Breakpoints
                     choose system calls at whose entry the process stops
           Continue  resume a stopped process (F5)
           Step      resume and stop at the next system call (F10)

       A stopped process is highlighted and its call has not run yet.
       Ctrl+Q closes the window and detaches.

SEE ALSO
       trace(1), ps(1)
